At Fri, 30 May 2003 18:17:03 -0200,
Tal Eisenberg wrote:
> 
> Hi, I own a Waveterminal 192M soundcard and recently moved to linux. I did 
> this partly because the sound apps and programming that I found for it seemed 
> really exciting and partly for the obvious microsoft-rules-the-world stuff. 
> Realizing that the card isn't supported on linux was a great disappointment.
> 
> I have lots of time on my hand, alot of programming experience, some C 
> experience and I know some stuff about the internal workings of the kernel. 
> Is there anything I can do to make the card work? 

above all, try to contact with the hardware vendor to get the hardware
info.
without it (especially the wiring of chips), it's quite hard to write
the driver, although the spec of the core chip (envy24ht) itself is
already available.


